  "body": "Stacked on #1252. Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n**What changed.** `site/content/guide/troubleshooting.md` gains three sections, every message grepped from `crates/`:\n- Importing a model: `file is empty`, `corrupt STL/OBJ/STEP: <reason>`, `unsupported file type: <ext>`, the IGES refusal, `model exceeds the import limit`, `imported mesh contains non-finite coordinates`, `the file states two length units (...)` (the wrong-scale entry), `Reduced fidelity: ...` and the reduced-fidelity operation refusal (sources: `geometry/import/mod.rs`, `commands/mod.rs`, `import/step_units.rs`, `model_fidelity.rs`).\n- Turning: `<Op> needs a turning insert, ...` (`operation/generate.rs`), `the part's axis of revolution is not the lathe spindle` (`spindle_law.rs`), the lathe-post refusals (`lathe_voice.rs`).\n- Plasma: `a plasma profile mounts a plasma torch` (`plasma_op.rs`), `the plasma laws have no toolpath to judge` and the \"3D stock sim does not run\" note (`posting_plasma.rs`).\n- Wire/sinker EDM: no operation refusal text exists on main yet, so not added; the page says so.\n\n**Convention.** Backticked spans in `###` headings are message stems; `<...>` and `...` are placeholders (documented in a comment at the top of the page source).\n\n**Test.** `crates/app/tests/docs_troubleshooting.rs::troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources` reads the page, extracts the stems and fails naming any not found in `crates/*/src`. It already caught one drifted stem from #1252 (`rubs the part`, the source says `rubs the {}`), fixed here. No xtask change, so no PROCESS_VERSION bump.\n\n**Gate.** `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/1244-docs-troubleshooting` green on the final head; clippy -D warnings clean on the test.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1253\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
